{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-807d03a5b9b1aaf1", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# TTSDS2: Resources and Benchmark for Evaluating Human-Quality Text to Speech Systems\narXiv: 2506.19441\nAuthors: \nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of TTSDS2, a more robust and improved version of the Text to Speech Distribution Score for evaluating synthetic speech.\n  2. Demonstration that TTSDS2 is the only metric out of 16 compared to achieve a Spearman correlation above 0.50 with subjective scores across all evaluated domains.\n  3. Release of a dataset containing over 11,000 subjective opinion score ratings for evaluating synthetic speech close to real speech.\n  4. Release of an automated pipeline for continually recreating a multilingual test dataset to prevent data contamination.\n  5. Release of a continually updated benchmark for evaluating Text to Speech systems across 14 languages.\n\nTags: Eval/嵌入, Eval/基准", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ae62c58e-653f-4e16-8918-4e1af589ac7f", "uuid": "bedb6899-f8f7-4516-bc12-6e6a7ed7aa0a", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T11:14:03.648Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# TTSDS2: Resources and Benchmark for Evaluating Human-Quality Text to Speech Systems\narXiv: 2506.19441\nAuthors: \nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of TTSDS2, a more robust and improved version of the Text to Speech Distribution Score for evaluating synthetic speech.\n  2. Demonstration that TTSDS2 is the only metric out of 16 compared to achieve a Spearman correlation above 0.50 with subjective scores across all evaluated domains.\n  3. Release of a dataset containing over 11,000 subjective opinion score ratings for evaluating synthetic speech close to real speech.\n  4. Release of an automated pipeline for continually recreating a multilingual test dataset to prevent data contamination.\n  5. Release of a continually updated benchmark for evaluating Text to Speech systems across 14 languages.\n\nTags: Eval/嵌入, Eval/基准", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-91d1ef705be7ad6d", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Emotion-Aligned Generation in Diffusion Text to Speech Models via Preference-Guided Optimization\narXiv: 2509.25416\nAuthors: Jiacheng Shi, Hongfei Du, Yangfan He, Y. Alicia Hong, Ye Gao\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose EASPO, a stepwise alignment framework that reformulates preference optimization as a local, time-conditioned task, replacing the flawed assumption that all intermediate states on a preferred trajectory are equally valid.\n  2. By aligning win/lose candidates at each denoising step from a shared latent, EASPO enables stepwise-controllable emotion shaping throughout the generation process.\n  3. We introduce EASPM, a time-aware reward model that directly scores emotional expressiveness and prosody on noisy intermediate states, enabling dense, temporally grounded preference learning and on-the-fly scoring.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ae62c58e-653f-4e16-8918-4e1af589ac7f", "uuid": "e1f663e6-d6f2-472e-b456-52c58a1fc20b", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T11:14:03.937Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Emotion-Aligned Generation in Diffusion Text to Speech Models via Preference-Guided Optimization\narXiv: 2509.25416\nAuthors: Jiacheng Shi, Hongfei Du, Yangfan He, Y. Alicia Hong, Ye Gao\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose EASPO, a stepwise alignment framework that reformulates preference optimization as a local, time-conditioned task, replacing the flawed assumption that all intermediate states on a preferred trajectory are equally valid.\n  2. By aligning win/lose candidates at each denoising step from a shared latent, EASPO enables stepwise-controllable emotion shaping throughout the generation process.\n  3. We introduce EASPM, a time-aware reward model that directly scores emotional expressiveness and prosody on noisy intermediate states, enabling dense, temporally grounded preference learning and on-the-fly scoring.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-RL优化", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-98cb430f1e50dc63", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# GLM-4-Voice: Towards Intelligent and Human-Like End-to-End Spoken Chatbot\narXiv: 2412.02612\nAuthors: Aohan Zeng, Zhengxiao Du, Mingdao Liu, Kedong Wang, Shengmin Jiang, Lei Zhao, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of an ultra-low bitrate (175bps), single-codebook speech tokenizer with 12.5Hz frame rate derived from an ASR model by incorporating a vector-quantized bottleneck into the encoder.\n  2. Synthesis of speech-text interleaved data from existing text pre-training corpora using a text-to-token model to efficiently transfer knowledge from text to speech modalities.\n  3. Continuation of pre-training from the GLM-4-9B text language model on a combination of unsupervised speech, interleaved speech-text, and supervised speech-text data, scaling up to 1 trillion tokens to achieve state-of-the-art performance in speech language modeling and spoken question answering.\n  4. Fine-tuning of the pre-trained model with high-quality conversational speech data using a \"streaming thoughts\" template to generate seamless, low-latency, and human-like spoken responses with controllable vocal nuances.\n  5. Demonstration of superior performance compared to existing spoken chatbot baselines in both conversational ability and speech quality while supporting bilingual Chinese and English interactions.\n\nTags: LALM, 压缩, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/音频标记-融合, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义, TTS/功能-流式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ae62c58e-653f-4e16-8918-4e1af589ac7f", "uuid": "993683e5-69e7-4781-bd2d-14275bf6aca1", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T11:14:04.206Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# GLM-4-Voice: Towards Intelligent and Human-Like End-to-End Spoken Chatbot\narXiv: 2412.02612\nAuthors: Aohan Zeng, Zhengxiao Du, Mingdao Liu, Kedong Wang, Shengmin Jiang, Lei Zhao, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of an ultra-low bitrate (175bps), single-codebook speech tokenizer with 12.5Hz frame rate derived from an ASR model by incorporating a vector-quantized bottleneck into the encoder.\n  2. Synthesis of speech-text interleaved data from existing text pre-training corpora using a text-to-token model to efficiently transfer knowledge from text to speech modalities.\n  3. Continuation of pre-training from the GLM-4-9B text language model on a combination of unsupervised speech, interleaved speech-text, and supervised speech-text data, scaling up to 1 trillion tokens to achieve state-of-the-art performance in speech language modeling and spoken question answering.\n  4. Fine-tuning of the pre-trained model with high-quality conversational speech data using a \"streaming thoughts\" template to generate seamless, low-latency, and human-like spoken responses with controllable vocal nuances.\n  5. Demonstration of superior performance compared to existing spoken chatbot baselines in both conversational ability and speech quality while supporting bilingual Chinese and English interactions.\n\nTags: LALM, 压缩, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/音频标记-融合, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义, TTS/功能-流式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
